/dblp.org/rec/journals/corr/WuLHZ13\n\nGaofei Wu, Nian Li, Tor Helleseth, Yuqing Zhang:\nMore Classes of Complete Permutation Polynomials over $\\F_q$. CoRR abs/1312.4716 (2013)\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nExtended framework for constructing (complete) permutations by specifying their coordinate functions (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/345647881_Extended_framework_for_constructing_complete_permutations_by_specifying_their_coordinate_functions)\nciteturn0search6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 months ago; On monomial complete permutation polynomials ... Some previous characterization results by Wu et al. for n=4 are also made more explicit by providing a complete list of a's such that axd is a CPP.\n  * Rohit Gupta\n  * Rajendra Kumar Sharma\n\nLet F-q denote the finite field of order q. In this paper, some new classes of permutation polynomials of the form (x(pm) - x + delta)(s) + x over F-p2m are obtained by determining the number of solutions of certain equations.\n\nView\n\nShow abstract\n\nOn monomial complete permutation polynomials\n\nArticle\n\n  * Sep 2016\n  * FINITE FIELDS TH APP\n\n  * Daniele Bartoli\n  * Massimo Giulietti\n  * Giovanni Zini\n\nWe investigate monomials axd over the finite field with q elements Fq, in the case where the degree d is equal to +1 with q=(q′)n for some n. For n=6 we explicitly list all a's for which axd is a complete permutation polynomial (CPP) over Fq. Some previous characterization results by Wu et al. for n=4 are also made more explicit by providing a complete list of a's such that axd is a CPP. For odd n, we show that if q is large enough with respect to n then axd cannot be a CPP over Fq, unless q is even, n≡3(mod4), and the trace TrFq/Fq′(a−1) is equal to 0.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTop arXiv papers (https://scirate.com/?date=2026-09-24&page=68&range=7)\nciteturn0search7 [wordlim: 200] Published